<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <MongoGenericRepositoryVersion>12.2.0</MongoGenericRepositoryVersion>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
    The entity's key is no longer trimmed on write.

    Fixed:
    - Add, AddRange and both Update overloads trimmed every string property, the Id included. A key with surrounding whitespace was stored under a trimmed key the caller did not hold, while Get, Delete and the id filters never trimmed. The Id and whichever member the serializer stores as _id are now written and matched exactly as passed.
    - Update filtered on the trimmed key, so it missed a document stored under the untrimmed one and, with IsUpsert, created a second document. It now matches by the untouched key; the same applies to the bulk Update.
    - AddRange and the bulk Update enumerate their sequence once. A lazy projection used to run twice: AddRange inserted untrimmed copies, and a mutating projection applied its change twice.
    - Static string properties are no longer trimmed.

    Added:
    - [NoTrim] keeps a string property out of the trimming, for values whose whitespace carries meaning: natural keys outside the id, hashes, signatures.

    Behaviour change:
    - Only keys with leading or trailing whitespace are affected. Documents written by earlier versions are stored under the trimmed key: an Update built from untrimmed input now misses them and, with IsUpsert, creates a second document. Normalise keys before building them if that is what you want.

    See CHANGELOG.md for the full notes.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    
    <!-- Gemeinsame Metadaten für alle Pakete -->
    <Authors>Timm Bremekamp</Authors>
    <Company>FM-Gruppe</Company>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/emuuu/MongoRepository</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageIcon>mongorepository_logo.png</PackageIcon>
    <Copyright>Copyright © $(Authors) $([System.DateTime]::Now.Year)</Copyright>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>